        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first player (or team) to reach 110 points. Each trick is worth 5 points; the holder of the highest trump in play gets an extra 5 points.',
          gameplay: "Bidding (10, 15, 20, 25, or 60) starts left of dealer; dealer may 'take' by equalling the bid. Highest bidder picks up the five-card kitty, discards five, and names trump (no robbing). Player to dealer's left leads; same card ranking as Twenty-Five (5 of trump highest, then J, then A of hearts).",
          keyRules: [
            'Bids: 10, 15, 20, 25, 60; dealer can take by equalling',
            'Bidder takes kitty, discards 5, names trump',
            '5 points per trick; +5 for highest trump in play',
            'First to 110 wins',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Bid according to hand strength and trump potential; remember card ranking (5, J, A♥, then K-Q and numerals; red suits 'highest best', black 'lowest best'). The 5 of trump and J of trump are the top trumps; A of hearts is always trump.",
          intermediate: 'Competing with dealer: dealer can take by equalling, so bids can be pushed up. Holding the highest trump gives +5; time when you play it. In 110, reaching the target in the same deal—who took tricks first can decide the winner.',
          advanced: 'Bid 60 only when you can win all five tricks. If you bid lower and make all tricks you score 30 (five tricks + highest trump), not 60. Track who is close to 110 and whether to bid to win or to block.',
          tips: [
            'Same ranking as Twenty-Five: learn 5, J, A♥ as top trumps and red high / black low in non-trump.',
            'Bidder names trump after taking kitty (or before, in some variants).',
            'First to 110 wins; last hand is played out to see if bid succeeds.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
